{
  "id": "b2-e11-money-and-consumerism",
  "level": "B2",
  "version": 1,
  "topic": "Money and consumerism",
  "parts": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "title": "Interview",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "p1-intro",
          "kind": "narration",
          "text": "Good evening. First of all, we'd like to know something about you.",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e11-money-and-consumerism/p1-intro.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4400
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-q1",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "A",
          "text": "Candidate A, what do you usually spend your money on?",
          "durationSec": 25,
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e11-money-and-consumerism/p1-q1.mp3",
          "audioMs": 3800
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-q2",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "B",
          "text": "Candidate B, do you prefer to buy things in shops or online?",
          "durationSec": 25,
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e11-money-and-consumerism/p1-q2.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4800
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-q3",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "A",
          "text": "Candidate A, have you ever bought something you later regretted?",
          "durationSec": 30,
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e11-money-and-consumerism/p1-q3.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4400
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-q4",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "B",
          "text": "Candidate B, how important is it for you to save money?",
          "durationSec": 30,
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e11-money-and-consumerism/p1-q4.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4100
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "title": "Long turn",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "p2-intro",
          "kind": "narration",
          "text": "In this part of the test, I'm going to give each of you two photographs. I'd like you to talk about them on your own for about a minute, and also to answer a question about your partner's photographs.",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e11-money-and-consumerism/p2-intro.mp3",
          "audioMs": 13000
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-a",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "A",
          "durationSec": 60,
          "assets": [
            "b2-e11-a1",
            "b2-e11-a2"
          ],
          "text": "Candidate A, your photographs show people dealing with objects they own or want. Compare the photographs, and say why the people might have made these choices.",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e11-money-and-consumerism/p2-a.mp3",
          "audioMs": 10500
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-a-follow",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "B",
          "durationSec": 30,
          "text": "Candidate B, would you prefer to buy new things or repair old ones? Why?",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e11-money-and-consumerism/p2-a-follow.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5800
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-b",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "B",
          "durationSec": 60,
          "assets": [
            "b2-e11-b1",
            "b2-e11-b2"
          ],
          "text": "Candidate B, your photographs show people shopping. Compare the photographs, and say how carefully the people are choosing what to buy.",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e11-money-and-consumerism/p2-b.mp3",
          "audioMs": 9000
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-b-follow",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "A",
          "durationSec": 30,
          "text": "Candidate A, how do you decide what to buy?",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e11-money-and-consumerism/p2-b-follow.mp3",
          "audioMs": 3500
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "title": "Collaborative task",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "p3-intro",
          "kind": "narration",
          "text": "Now I'd like you to talk about something together for about two minutes. Here are some things that influence what people buy, and a question for you to discuss.",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e11-money-and-consumerism/p3-intro.mp3",
          "audioMs": 10000
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-discuss",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "both",
          "durationSec": 120,
          "diagram": "b2-e11-money-and-consumerism",
          "text": "Talk to each other about this question: How might these things affect what people decide to buy?",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e11-money-and-consumerism/p3-discuss.mp3",
          "audioMs": 6600
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-decide",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "both",
          "durationSec": 60,
          "diagram": "b2-e11-money-and-consumerism",
          "text": "Now you have about a minute to decide together. Which has the biggest influence on young people?",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e11-money-and-consumerism/p3-decide.mp3",
          "audioMs": 6700
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "title": "Discussion",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "p4-intro",
          "kind": "narration",
          "text": "Now I'd like to ask you some more questions about spending and shopping.",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e11-money-and-consumerism/p4-intro.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4900
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q1",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "both",
          "durationSec": 50,
          "text": "Some people say that we all buy far more than we need. What do you think?",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e11-money-and-consumerism/p4-q1.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4900
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q2",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "A",
          "durationSec": 45,
          "text": "Candidate A, do you think advertising is always honest?",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e11-money-and-consumerism/p4-q2.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4300
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q3",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "B",
          "durationSec": 45,
          "text": "Candidate B, how can people learn to be more careful with their money?",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e11-money-and-consumerism/p4-q3.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4600
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q4",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "both",
          "durationSec": 50,
          "text": "Is it a good idea for shops to have big sales?",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e11-money-and-consumerism/p4-q4.mp3",
          "audioMs": 3600
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q5",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "A",
          "durationSec": 45,
          "text": "Candidate A, do you think people are happier when they own more things?",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e11-money-and-consumerism/p4-q5.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4700
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
